54717" :question/problem "The inequality $1\\le x\\le 5$ can be expressed in interval notation as" :question/worked-solution "Every inequality can be expressed as an interval. We use the following notations:\n\n- Parentheses $()$ if the endpoints are *not* included.\n\n- Brackets $[]$ if the endpoints *are* included.\n\nOur inequality contains only \"or equal to\" symbols. So, the endpoints $1$ and $5$ *are* included. \n\n$$\n1\\,\\,\\le \\,\\,x\\,\\,\\le \\,\\,5\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express our inequality in interval notation as follows:\n\n$$\n[1,5]\n$$\n\nMore formally, we can also write\n\n$$\nx\\in [1,5].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-37038cfb-4364-58c7-8027-27793c04b330"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-37038cfb-4364-58c7-8027-27793c04b330" :answer-field/id #uuid "37038cfb-4364-58c7-8027-27793c04b330" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2f9055f6-bbd2-57f5-867f-46b21bf3bb97" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e83c5b5b-2113-5fab-83c6-66a9ffcc9dbf" "answer-aa39e0ad-a191-5047-bc57-3b582cadb1c3" "answer-c6fd135d-d86a-5987-9de8-d466c75f9138" "answer-1bd995a9-b989-5eb9-a1bd-bb739025a499" "answer-2f9055f6-bbd2-57f5-867f-46b21bf3bb97"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e83c5b5b-2113-5fab-83c6-66a9ffcc9dbf" :answer/id #uuid "e83c5b5b-2113-5fab-83c6-66a9ffcc9dbf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-\\infty ,5]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aa39e0ad-a191-5047-bc57-3b582cadb1c3" :answer/id #uuid "aa39e0ad-a191-5047-bc57-3b582cadb1c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1,5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c6fd135d-d86a-5987-9de8-d466c75f9138" :answer/id #uuid "c6fd135d-d86a-5987-9de8-d466c75f9138" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1,5]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1bd995a9-b989-5eb9-a1bd-bb739025a499" :answer/id #uuid